/-!
# Open direct-image finiteness for all-continuous algebraic-closure coefficients

Source: blueprint main-20261015, sec-six-functors-basics/sk-thm-sf-ctf-stability,
sk-thm-sf-ctf-stability-direct-images.proof.md, paragraph (3), retained all-continuous case
(blueprint: lem-sfb-continuous-algcl-open-finiteness).

The coefficient ring has all continuous functions into the normed algebraic closure as
sections. The assertion concerns the ordinary total right derived module direct image
and bounded cohomology with finite constant local models on constructible strata.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

attribute [instance] Profinite.continuousMapRingObjOfUniverseMonObj
  Profinite.isCommMonObj_continuousMapRingObjOfUniverse

open CategoryTheory
open scoped CategoryTheory.Obj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

/-- Ordinary open direct image preserves bounded constructibility with finite constant
local models for all-continuous algebraic-closure coefficients. The normed algebra
structure specifies the extension of the ell-adic absolute value to the algebraic closure.

Source: blueprint main-20261015, sk-thm-sf-ctf-stability-direct-images.proof.md,
paragraph (3), retained all-continuous open-image finiteness input
(blueprint: lem-sfb-continuous-algcl-open-finiteness).

Proof plan:
1. The finite-type-over-Noetherian and qcqs-over-affine lemmas make the schemes and
strata Noetherian and qcqs. By lem-sfb-continuous-qbar-constructible-generators the
bounded finite-constant-model objects form a replete triangulated class, generated by
locally closed extensions a_!L of lisse modules in degree zero. On bounded-below
objects the ordinary derived pushforward agrees with its bounded-below version by
sk-def-sfb-module-derived-pushpull. It is triangulated by
lem-weil-pbc-derived-direct-image-triangulated. It suffices to treat these generators.
2. Apply lem-sfb-continuous-algcl-stratified-finite-models to L and refine its finite
stratification by lem-sfb-noetherian-good-stratification-refinement, using locally
closed pullbacks so the finite-field models restrict along actual scheme morphisms.
The open layer and closed complement, with the exact localization sequence of
lem-weil-pbc-proetale-ringed-open-closed, give by induction a finite extension filtration
with pieces b_!(B_V tensor over A_E,V N), where N is lisse over one finite extension E.
An open layer with several disjoint strata contributes their finite direct sum. Exact
a_! transports this to a finite triangle filtration; the empty complement contributes zero.
3. Set C = (a_!b_!N)[0]. By lem-sfb-scalar-model-immersion-extension it is bounded
constructible over A_E, retaining its old strata and the zero model on complements.
The field/free clause of lem-sfb-scalar-model-finite-flat-resolution identifies derived
and ordinary scalar extension of N. Factor a,b as open then closed immersions and use
both clauses of lem-sfb-condensed-support-projection-formula to identify B_U tensor^L C
with G = a_!b_!(B_V tensor N)[0]. The comparison is B-linear: on local pure tensors it
preserves the product bn, so the isomorphism holds in B-modules.
4. Scalar extension carries a bounded constructible A_E-complex M with cohomology in
[r,s] to a bounded constructible B-complex in the same interval. Refine the finitely
many cohomology stratifications to one. The field case of the finite-flat-resolution
lemma makes its cohomology locally finite free. Evaluation and coevaluation descend
from local trivializations. The truncation triangles of lem-weil-pbc-truncation-triangle
and stability in lem-zl-condensed-dualizable-local-perfect-models make M dualizable
on each stratum, and that lemma supplies local perfect E-complexes. Restriction commutes
with scalar extension by lem-weil-pbc-ringed-topoi-derived-tensor-pullback. Their scalar
extensions have the same cohomological interval: finite vector-space complexes split
into cohomology and contractible pairs. Discard empty cover members. Exact restriction
to all strata detects zero by repeated open/closed localization, proving the global
interval and finite constant models. This does not assert flatness on arbitrary modules.
5. Apply the finite-E clause of lem-sfb-rational-open-direct-image-constructible to C.
It gives M = Rj_*,A_E C bounded constructible. Step 4 treats its scalar extension.
The canonical isomorphism of lem-sfb-continuous-algcl-open-scalar-comparison identifies
that extension with Rj_*,B(B_U tensor^L C), hence with Rj_*,B G by step 3. The finite
filtrations and triangulated argument in steps 1--2 prove the result for K. Minima and
maxima of the finitely many bounds give boundedness. Identity and empty open immersions
give the identity and zero functors, respectively.
-/
theorem constantModelBoundedConstructible_continuous_algcl_open_direct_image
    (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    (Ω : Type u) [NormedField Ω] [NormedAlgebra ℚ_[ℓ] Ω] [IsAlgClosure ℚ_[ℓ] Ω]
    (k : Type u) [Field k] [Fact (ringChar k).Prime] [Fact (ringChar k ≠ ℓ)]
    {U X : Scheme.{u}} [U.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (U ↘ Spec (.of k))] [QuasiCompact (U ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [IsSeparated (U ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] [QuasiCompact (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    [IsSeparated (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (j : U ⟶ X) [j.IsOver (Spec (.of k))] [IsOpenImmersion j] [QuasiCompact j]
    (K : DerivedCategory (Mod (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology U) Ab.{u + 1})
      (condensedRingObj (Profinite.continuousMapRingObjOfUniverse.{u, u} Ω) U)))
    (hK : constantModelBoundedConstructible
      (Profinite.continuousMapRingObjOfUniverse.{u, u} Ω) U K) :
    constantModelBoundedConstructible (Profinite.continuousMapRingObjOfUniverse.{u, u} Ω) X
      ((CondensedRing.moduleObjectDerivedPushforward
        (Profinite.continuousMapRingObjOfUniverse.{u, u} Ω) j).obj K) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale
